            {
              "_key": "k119",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k120",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Switching Regimes When You File",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k121",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k122",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "If you have no business or professional income, you choose your regime fresh every year in your return, whatever you told HR. For FY 2025-26, you can opt for the old regime only in a return filed by the due date under section 139(1) of the 1961 Act, normally 31 July. A belated return is taxed under the new regime. From tax year 2026-27, the same choice is made in the return under section 263(1) of the Income-tax Act, 2025.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "What happens when Form 16 and your return use different regimes",
              "headers": [
                "Form 16 regime",
                "Regime in your return",
                "Likely result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k124",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Old",
                    "New, and new is cheaper",
                    "Excess TDS comes back as a refund"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k126",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "New",
                    "Old, with enough deductions to make it cheaper",
                    "Excess TDS comes back as a refund. Keep proofs, since Form 16 will not show your claims."
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k128",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "New",
                    "Old, without enough deductions",
                    "Tax is higher, so you pay the balance as self-assessment tax before filing"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k129"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "warning",
              "text": "The yearly switch is only for people without business or professional income. If you also freelance or run a business, the rules are stricter: opting out needs Form 10-IEA by the due date, and you can switch back to the old regime only once in your lifetime.",
              "_key": "k130"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k131",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
