              "prompt": "Arvind earns ₹15,00,000 gross salary in the new regime. His employer starts contributing ₹84,000 a year to NPS, which is 14% of his basic salary, deductible under section 80CCD(2). By how much does his tax including cess fall?",
              "correctValue": 13104,
              "tolerance": 1,
              "unit": "₹",
              "explanation": "Without NPS: taxable ₹14,25,000, slab tax ₹93,750, with cess ₹97,500. With NPS: taxable ₹13,41,000, slab tax ₹81,150, with cess ₹84,396. Saving: ₹97,500 minus ₹84,396 = ₹13,104.",
              "_key": "k135"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "fillInTheBlank",
              "title": "The zero-tax salary",
              "textWithBlank": "Under the new regime for FY 2025-26, a salaried employee with no other income pays no tax on gross salary of up to ₹___.",
              "correctAnswers": [
                "12,75,000",
